1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Before we go deep on features, let's map the whole app once — the sidebar, the composer, and the per-chat panel — so later episodes can dive in without stopping to explain where things are.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:10,600
At the top: New chat for typing, and New call for a spoken conversation — yes, you can talk to it, that's Module 5.

3
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:14,000
Below them, a search box that looks inside your conversations, not just their titles.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,062
Then Projects — think of a project as a workspace that scopes your chats and gives shared instructions; full episode later.

5
00:00:19,062 --> 00:00:24,000
Under Chats, every conversation has a menu: pin it, rename, file it in a folder, duplicate, snapshot, export, or delete.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:25,731
Two grouped sections hold the power features.

7
00:00:25,731 --> 00:00:29,154
Library is about models: Discover to get them, My Models, Compare, Evals, and Benchmarks.

8
00:00:29,154 --> 00:00:33,654
Automation is about capability: Agents, Skills, Knowledge, Tools, Workflows, Schedules, MCP Servers, and the Browser.

9
00:00:33,654 --> 00:00:35,000
Each of these gets its own episode.

10
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,724
Down at the composer you've got Attach, Dictate, Compact, and Regenerate.

11
00:00:37,724 --> 00:00:43,246
And on the right, the per-chat panel — this is where each conversation sets its own model, temperature, system prompt, tools, and working directory.

12
00:00:43,246 --> 00:00:45,000
Settings that live with the chat, not globally.

13
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:46,388
Finally, Settings — eight panels.

14
00:00:46,388 --> 00:00:49,879
The nicest touch: the search box matches on what a setting does, not just its name.

15
00:00:49,879 --> 00:00:51,519
Type “interrupt” and it finds barge-in.

16
00:00:51,519 --> 00:00:54,000
If you can describe the behavior, you can find the setting.

17
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:55,298
You can now find anything in the app.

18
00:00:55,298 --> 00:01:00,000
Next module builds the mental model — what actually happens when you send a turn, so nearly every “why did it do that” answers itself.

